    /* THE MAIN RUNWAY PLATE, OVERLAPPED BY 128 (drop 0724cx).
       I tiled the EXIT plate by butting it, on the strength of its top ROW matching its bottom
       ROW. That was the wrong measurement twice over: its top and bottom 4 rows are fully
       TRANSPARENT, so butting left a black gap, and its own top-128 band differs from its
       bottom-128 by 24 — it was never the repeating piece.
       nst4b_run IS: its top 128 equals its bottom 128 at 0.000, which is exactly what the pack's
       seam_overlap:128 describes. Stepping by (H-128) overlaps those identical bands and the join
       disappears. The runway can now be any length. */
